{
  "format": "evn-blocks",
  "version": 2,
  "title": "I2C: every block",
  "needs": "an EVN IMU module (MPU-6500) on I2C port 1",
  "description": "Every I2C block once, on the EVN IMU module (an MPU-6500): the addresses that answer, whether one answers at 0x68, its WHO_AM_I register (0x75, which reads 0x70 = 112), its acceleration and temperature as signed 16-bit numbers, 14 raw bytes of acceleration, temperature and turn rate as a list, and a write that wakes the chip (PWR_MGMT_1, 0x6B), put back as it was at the end. Nothing is written unless WHO_AM_I says it is an MPU-6500.",
  "workspace": {
    "blocks": {
      "languageVersion": 0,
